<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75576" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσομαι</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσε</span>) 
			Ep.
		 Verb, used only in pres. and impf.
		without augm., pres. (I.-<i><span class="en">
			E.
		</span></i>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>oq[uglide]-yo-</i>)
			corresponding to fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψομαι</span> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψ</span>) : 
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσω</span> only <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				562.6
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				673.11
			</span></i> : prop. <i>see, look,</i> as in <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.318
			</span></i>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμμασι λοξὸν ὑποδρὰξ ὀσσομένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
				</span></i>
			<i>Fr.anon.</i><i><span class="en">
				63
			</span></i>, and in the compd. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προτιόσσομαι</span> (q.v.) : but mostly, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>see in spirit</i> or <i>with the mind's eye,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσσόμενος πατέρ᾽ ἐσθλὸν ἐνὶ φρεσίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.115
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				20.81
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>presage, have foreboding of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακὰ δ᾽ ὄσσετο θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.374
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				18.154
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσοντο γὰρ ἄλγεα θυμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.224
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> by imparting
			such presages to others, <i>forebode,</i> used only of evil, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς ὅτε πορφύρῃ πέλαγος μέγα κύματι
					κωφῷ ὀσσόμενον λιγέων ἀνέμων λαιψηρὰ κέλευθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.17
				</span></i>
			 ; esp. by look or mien, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάκ᾽
				ὀσσόμενος</span>
			<i>boding</i> evil <i>by his looks,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1.105
			</span></i> ; of two eagles, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσοντο ὄλεθρον</span>
			<i>boded</i> death, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.152
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μὲν γάρ τοι ἐγὼ κακὸν ὀσσομένη
					τόδ᾽ ἱκάνω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.172
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				551
			</span></i>.</div>
